{
  "requirement": "The SDK presents node inputs using the returned value's `NodeContents::format`\nunder {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nIts text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet contents = domain.node_content(&node_id)?;\nlet text = contents.format();\n```\n\nLoading and fallible preparation occur in `Domain::node_content` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`. For inputs queued on an ask\nbuilder, these failures return `ValidationError::Graph`. During a `read_node`\ntool call, they are returned to the agent as a tool error, so it can continue\nand recover.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`. I did not read implementation source. I judged the test text only, and I did not read the `distinct_pages` helper or the `ParallelConversations` and `Script` providers.\n\nObligations and the tests that cover them:\n\n1. **Inputs are presented through the returned value's `NodeContents::format`.**\n   - `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` gives the `Memory` domain a custom formatter that outputs \"formatted input: …\". It asserts that the first user message sent to the agent contains \"formatted input: source\". Raw content or a different rendering would fail this.\n   - `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` checks that the domain's node contents appear in the agent message, in order.\n   - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` checks the rendered inputs the agent receives, including their order and repetition.\n   - `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` runs with the custom `distinct_pages` formatter. I did not confirm that it exercises `read_node` rendering.\n\n2. **Text and fingerprint describe the same retained observation.**\n   - `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` in `tests/contracts.rs` reads a snapshot and then changes the underlying contents. It asserts that `format()` still returns \"before\". It also asserts that the snapshot's fingerprint value is \"before\" and equals `content.fingerprint()`. Only one read occurs.\n   - In the ask tests, the recorded `Dependency::Node` fingerprint (\"source\", or the node text) is consistent with the rendered text.\n   - `domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement` in `src/sdk.rs` checks that `HabeasNodeContent` formats the already-read text without re-resolving the source.\n\n3. **Failures on an ask builder return `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n   - `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` sets `fail_read`, `fail_edges` and `fail_prepare` in turn. It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"read\"))`, `Graph(\"edges\")` and `Graph(\"render\")`. It also asserts that no agent request is made and that no dependencies are recorded after the preparation failure. This covers both the loading and the fallible-preparation failure classes.\n\n4. **During `read_node`, failures go back to the agent as a tool error so it can recover.**\n   - `node_preparation_tool_errors_allow_recovery_without_recording_undelivered_contents` makes the node-contents preparation return an error. It asserts that:\n     - the next request carries a single tool result with `is_error`;\n     - the tool name is `read_node`;\n     - the content is the error text;\n     - the agent then submits successfully;\n     - no dependency is recorded.\n   - Loading and preparation failures both come back through the same `Domain::node_content` error, so one preparation-failure test covers the tool path.\n\nThe \"completes without further resource reads\" clause belongs to `node_content.format`, which is cited context here and not reassessed. The loading and preparation obligation belongs to `node_content`, which is also cited context. All the tests carry `{test}` references to the subject, so there is no marking gap.",
  "references": "f6ca580b7ad3955509357366e0e56b0d72b32452bd72e328b9bd2bf30481a0de",
